      "summaryMarkdown": "All eight criteria are met. `entry_dependencies` resolves keys against normal declarations only (rename, target table, features, default-features, optional, path/git/registry) with both errors; features are forwarded generically with no invented `devkit`; every entry crate is seeded from the workspace lock only when the project has one (checked before the graph's `cargo metadata` can write it), and the web block keeps only wasm-bindgen/futures; patches are selected by the single feature-aware `AppGraph` and rendered as TOML into all three entry crates; `--android-devkit` checks the `devkit` feature before the toolchain and the bridge message names no tool. Each task has its own new test group; finding s2-lock-no-workspace-lock-with-patch is resolved and covered by `tests/app_entry_lockfile.rs`.",
